From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: tanjilbhuiyan <tanjilbhuiyan@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 23:21:01 +0600
Subject: [PATCH 11/14] arm64: dts: exynos9610-a50: add the ABOX DMA,
 interfaces and sound card

Add the ABOX children of the stock DT under the ABOX node: RDMA0-7 (RDMA5
the compress channel with its mailbox), WDMA0-4, UAIF0/1/2/4, DSIF, SPDY
and the effect block, with the mainline CMU_DISPAUD UAIF/DSIF/FM dividers
and their ABOX BCLK gates. Pin control for the I2S buses is left out; no
pin changes until the codec and amplifier are added.

Add the sound card node with the link layout of the stock DTBO: DMA front
ends on the ABOX DAIs, back ends on the interfaces and SIFS0-2, every back
end on the dummy codec for now, UAIF4 as clock consumer (UAIF0 slave).
The Bluetooth (SCO), VSS, debug and synchronized-IPC children stay out.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Change-Id: Ibef98943fead84f2df909617bcf1d43f7c8dfde8
---
